From 9c61546ad709b22ff5397026d89c3f69249525ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:02:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Sketches of the clustering, the mask and the groups of
 clusters

Two hand-drawn figures in the science pages, computed on three catchments around
Piz Kesch (SRTM DEM of the Davos example, 100 m):
- clustering: features of each cell, k-means in feature space, 300 clusters on
  the map, with the scattered cells of one cluster in red;
- mask and groups: the mask of the catchments of interest, the groups raster,
  150 clusters with the mask only (29 cross a divide), and per catchment with
  n_g = ceil(N w_g) (none crosses a divide).

The text explains the mask and the groups: groups bound the clusters and share
N out by area or by clustering_group_weights; the features are standardised per
group; labels follow each other. A snippet computes a mean per catchment.

prepare_kesch.py builds the terrain (pyflwdir catchments, slope, aspect and svf
from topo_param), make_cluster_sketches.py the figures, with the maps of clusters
as PNG images. roughen.js rounds path coordinates to 0.1 px, which halves the
other figures. Also fix the k-means formula (no \boldsymbol) and a nested list.

